1866,Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1866 Arabic Hadees: 1136
1867,"A man from Banu Asad reported that he said: ""I and my family settled at Baqi' al-Gharqad. My family said to me: 'Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and ask him for something for us to eat.' And they kept mentioning their needs. So I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and found a man with him asking him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was saying: 'I do not find anything to give you.' So the man turned away from him in anger, saying: 'By my life, you indeed give to whom you wish.' The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: 'He becomes angry with me because I do not find anything to give him. Whoever among you asks while he has an uqiyah or its equivalent, he has asked importunately.' The Asadi said: 'So I said: A milch camel for us is better than an uqiyah.' Malik said: 'And the uqiyah is forty dirhams.' He said: 'So I returned and did not ask him. Then barley and raisins were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) after that, and he distributed to us from them until Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, made us self-sufficient."""
1868,"Abu Jurayy al-Hujaymi reported: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, we are a people from the desert dwellers, so teach us something that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, may benefit us with."" He said: ""Do not belittle any good deed, even if it is emptying your bucket into the vessel of the one seeking water, or speaking to your brother with a cheerful face. And beware of trailing the lower garment, for it is from arrogance, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not love arrogance. And if a man reviles you with what he knows about you, do not revile him with what you know about him, for his reward is for you and his sin is upon the one who said it."""
1869,Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1869 Arabic Hadees: 3568
